openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:3:Provide bounded query-time retrieval wording for explicit electric-actuation intent while retaining the tender's requested control state and existing matching semantics.
openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:9:For a catalog-domain tender query that explicitly requests a ball valve supplied with an electric actuator or explicitly requests a ball valve prepared for a future electric actuator, the system SHALL emit at most one distinct additive retrieval representation with catalog-native wording for that same state. The alternate SHALL retain the source query's product, DN, PN, material, connection, designation, and other explicit constraints.
openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:11:#### Scenario: Installed electric actuator request
openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:13:- **WHEN** a supported tender query explicitly states that an electric actuator is installed or supplied with the valve
openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:14:- **THEN** the system emits a distinct alternate containing installed-electric-actuator vocabulary while retaining the source constraints
openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:18:- **WHEN** a supported tender query explicitly states that the valve is for or prepared for an electric actuator
openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:19:- **THEN** the system emits a distinct alternate containing actuator-ready vocabulary and does not state that an actuator is installed
openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:23:The system SHALL NOT infer either electric control state from generic or ambiguous actuation wording. It SHALL retrieve with the source query regardless of alternate availability, preserve the source query for reranking and result text, preserve current fusion and candidate limits, and retain usable source-query candidates if alternate retrieval fails.
openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:25:#### Scenario: Ambiguous actuation wording
openspec/changes/cycle-15-actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/specs/actuation-intent-retrieval-expansion/spec.md:27:- **WHEN** a query contains only generic drive wording without an explicit installed-electric or actuator-ready signal
